    <div class="prose-thai">
      <h2>Your Week of Thai Keto Eating</h2>
      <p>One of the biggest challenges of keto is meal fatigue — eating the same things over and over. This 7-day Thai keto meal plan solves that problem. Every meal is inspired by authentic Thai flavors, every day stays under 25g net carbs, and most importantly, every dish is genuinely delicious.</p>

      <h2>Day 1: Getting Started</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Thai-style omelet (khai jiao) — crispy-edged omelet with fish sauce and green onions. Serve with sliced avocado. <em>4g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Leftover keto Thai green curry with cauliflower rice. <em>8g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Tom Yum soup with shrimp and mushrooms. Rich, spicy, and nearly zero-carb. <em>5g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 1 total:</strong> ~17g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 2: Curry Day</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Bulletproof Thai coffee — coffee blended with coconut oil and a dash of cardamom. <em>0g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Keto Thai red curry with chicken and green beans. <em>7g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Larb moo (Thai minced pork salad) wrapped in butter lettuce cups. <em>4g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 2 total:</strong> ~11g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 3: Street Food Favorites</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Two soft-boiled eggs with fish sauce, white pepper, and fresh cilantro. <em>1g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Pad kra pao (Thai basil stir-fry) with ground pork, served over cauliflower rice with a fried egg. <em>7g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Gai yang (Thai grilled chicken) with a spicy dipping sauce (nam jim jaew). Side of grilled zucchini. <em>5g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 3 total:</strong> ~13g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 4: Soup & Salad</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Coconut chia pudding with lime zest and a pinch of stevia. <em>4g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Tom kha gai (coconut chicken soup) — creamy, tangy, and deeply satisfying. <em>6g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Yum nua (Thai beef salad) with grilled flank steak, fresh herbs, and a spicy lime dressing. <em>5g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 4 total:</strong> ~15g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 5: Noodle Day</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Thai-style scrambled eggs with fish sauce, chili, and green onions. <em>2g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Keto Pad Thai with konjac noodles, shrimp, and crushed peanuts. <em>6g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Panang curry with beef and green beans. Rich, creamy, and slightly spicy. <em>6g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 5 total:</strong> ~14g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 6: Grill Day</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Avocado with fish sauce, lime, and chili flakes. <em>3g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Moo ping (Thai grilled pork skewers) with a cucumber salad. <em>4g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Pla neung manao (steamed fish with lime, garlic, and chili). Side of stir-fried bok choy. <em>5g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 6 total:</strong> ~12g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Day 7: Feast Day</h2>
      <p><strong>Breakfast:</strong> Keto Thai green smoothie — coconut milk, spinach, lime, ginger, and protein powder. <em>5g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Lunch:</strong> Massaman curry with chicken and cauliflower rice. The richest, most complex Thai curry. <em>8g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Dinner:</strong> Thai hot pot (suki) — cook thinly sliced beef, shrimp, and vegetables in a flavorful broth at the table. <em>6g net carbs</em></p>
      <p><strong>Day 7 total:</strong> ~19g net carbs</p>

      <h2>Meal Prep Tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Make curry bases ahead:</strong> Green and red curry pastes fried in coconut cream can be refrigerated for 5 days. Just add protein and vegetables when ready to eat.</li>
        <li><strong>Batch cook cauliflower rice:</strong> Make a big batch and freeze in portions. Reheat in a dry pan for best texture.</li>
        <li><strong>Prep aromatics:</strong> Blend lemongrass, galangal, garlic, and shallots into a paste and freeze in ice cube trays.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep konjac noodles ready:</strong> Pre-rinse and dry-fry a few packs. Store in the fridge for quick Pad Thai.</li>
      </ul>
